# PROBE TOPO -- not a thesis fabric.  Twin of scaleup_single_switch_64_4000Gbps
# with only the latencies doubled, to
# classify the ~141 ns constant floor of the ring baseline as latency- or
# serialisation-derived.  See model_checks/floor_probe.
# scaleup_single_switch_64_4000Gbps.topo
#
# Models an NVLink-class SCALE-UP domain as a single non-blocking crossbar:
# 64 hosts (GPUs) all attached to ONE ToR switch, every pair exactly one hop apart.
# Per-host link = 4000 Gbps; switch latency 300 ns, link 50 ns. 4000 Gbps is exactly
# 2 ps/B, chosen so the fabric link rate coincides with the receiver-NIC rate
# (-intranode_linkspeed 4000000) by construction, rather than leaning on htsim's
# integer-picosecond-per-byte rounding -- which also collapses 3600 Gbps (2.22 ps/B)
# to 2 ps/B. NVLink-aggregate class is ~3600-4000 Gbps; the two give identical timing.
#
# Encoding note: htsim's FatTree parser rejects Tiers=1 (fat_tree_topology.cpp), so a
# single switch is expressed as a DEGENERATE 2-tier fat-tree: Podsize == Nodes and
# Tier-0 Radix_Down == Nodes => exactly one ToR holds all hosts. The Tier-1 uplink
# (Radix_Up 1) is vestigial and carries no host<->host traffic (all pairs are same-ToR,
# one hop). Oversubscribed == Nodes keeps radix_down/radix_up == oversub (parser check).
#
# Scaled to 64 hosts for the INC-vs-ring speedup-vs-N sweep (D3).
Nodes 64
Tiers 2
Podsize 64

Tier 0
Downlink_speed_Gbps 4000
Radix_Down 64
Radix_Up 1
Downlink_Latency_ns 100
Switch_Latency_ns 600
Oversubscribed 64

Tier 1
Downlink_speed_Gbps 4000
Radix_Down 1
Downlink_Latency_ns 100
Switch_Latency_ns 600
